  "text": "Recipe: Instant Pot Khandvi\nCreator: Padma Subramanian\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: 1/2 cup plant based yogurt, 1 cup besan (chickpea flour), 1 1/2 cups water, Turmeric powder, 2 tsp green chilly & ginger paste, Asafoetida, Salt (optional), Cilantro, white sesame, mustard\nCooking methods: blend, pressure cook, no-cook, roast\nInstructions: + Whisk water & yogurt. Add ginger & green chilly paste, turmeric powder, asafoetida & salt. Whisk thoroughly. Add besan and whisk till no lumps.\n+ Keep in Instant Pot for 12 minutes manual. Quick release pressure.\n+ Give the hot cooked besan mixture a quick whisk and spread it on silicone mat when hot. Wait till it cools down and cut it into strips and roll it.\n+ Garnish with cilantro and dry roasted mustard seeds, sesame and asafoetida.\n+ Serve hot with green chaat chutney.\nNotes: A recipe with BEANS (besan), NUTS & SEEDS (almond milk), HERBS & SPICES (various).\nDHOKLA",
